00:35:14.700 --> 00:35:16.860
The actual tool I'm using
here is called Stern.

00:35:16.860 --> 00:35:18.780
It's a open source
Kubernetes logging

00:35:18.780 --> 00:35:20.700
tool that's super
helpful in that you

00:35:20.700 --> 00:35:23.970
can use regular expressions to
exclude certain types of logs,

00:35:23.970 --> 00:35:27.490
and you can also select
based on deployment.

00:35:27.490 --> 00:35:29.760
So you don't actually
need the pod name, which

00:35:29.760 --> 00:35:32.490
